<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Gelang-gelang</h1><p class="st-meta">1292 CE – 1293 CE · capital Daha</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The brief revival of Kediri under Jayakatwang, who killed King Kertanegara of Singhasari in 1292 and was overthrown by Raden Wijaya and a Mongol army.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayakatwang">Jayakatwang</a>, ruler of Gelang-gelang and a descendant of the kings of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kediri-kingdom">Kediri Kingdom</a>, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kertanegara">Kertanegara of Singhasari</a>. In 1292, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singhasari">Singhasari's</a> army was away in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, he attacked, killed Kertanegara and restored the old royal seat at Daha. The register names his state after his former fief.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayakatwang">Jayakatwang</a> ruled for barely a year. He pardoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kertanegara">Kertanegara's</a> son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raden-wijaya">Raden Wijaya</a>, who on the advice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arya-wiraraja">Arya Wiraraja</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-sumenep">Sumenep</a> pretended submission and was given land at Tarik, where he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1293 a Mongol fleet sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> to punish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kertanegara">Kertanegara</a> landed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raden-wijaya">Raden Wijaya</a> joined it, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayakatwang">Jayakatwang</a> at Daha and then turned on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, driving them out. Jayakatwang died in captivity, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> became the main power in Java.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1292 CE – 1293 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Maritime Southeast Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.41%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1292 CE – 1293 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Daha</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Jayakatwang</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism and Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Javanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gelanggelang, Kediri under Jayakatwang</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1292&amp;focus=gelang-gelang" aria-label="Gelang-gelang on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7952 2505 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Gelang-gelang lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8272 2761L8114 2731M8272 2761L7867 1005"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8114 2731h0M7867 1005h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8272 2761h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8272 2761h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Daha. <a href="/atlas?year=1292&amp;focus=gelang-gelang">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

